<p>Peru’s Congress voted to remove interim President José Jerí on Feb. 17, ending his four-month tenure. Lawmakers pointed to allegations involving undisclosed meetings with Chinese executives and business figures, alongside a preliminary investigation into corruption and influence peddling. The ouster adds a fresh layer of uncertainty weeks before Peru’s April 12 general election.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/KSSuZyvwqIiEfXEeA0eypJLvXxLlcnmzHu39my6tzrFLgR5SqeMpUxO3I3WhF86iuSikenqVN6alnS0BUT0s8QebU0sm2va5X-g9PN1SkH242_quYcIaFDhap-55LvAGvhV3wrEGsysM36cBmt-Qpsa9Q-B34v7sLQ03KLv8VDXbx3r7veGCgtUf-aBiLUJ2z1RZJ7J77Q8mjm0gTcCpONyIS0IIQAo-qF3P2ecUIvvabqL_w65sjOlTViwQmnissxdXKtoM32DfrdAKsg' alt='People gather after Peru&#x27;s Congress ousted President Jose Jeri in Lima on Feb. 17, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Vote tally: Congress approved Jerí’s removal 75–24, with three abstentions, according to multiple reports.</li><li>‘Chifagate’ label: The scandal picked up the nickname “Chifagate” after reports of late-night, unregistered meetings at a Chinese restaurant tied to a Chinese state contractor.</li><li>Succession context: Jerí took office last October, replacing Dina Boluarte after Congress removed her from the presidency.</li><li>Age profile: During his brief time in office, some coverage described Jerí as one of the world’s youngest heads of state.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Peru’s Congress: Lawmakers backed the removal after debating allegations tied to undisclosed meetings and a preliminary corruption and influence-peddling probe involving Chinese business figures. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/perus-congress-removes-interim-president-jose-jeri-as-he-faces-corruption-probe'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>José Jerí’s critics in media coverage: Some outlets described the vote as an unusually fast-track, or “express,” impeachment, arguing the scandal — and the timing — pushed Congress to move quickly. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/17/perus-president-ousted-in-express-impeachment-after-just-four-months'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>China-focused reporting: Coverage highlighted the China-linked angle of the allegations, including references to a Chinese state contractor and businessman Zhihua Yang. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/3343850/peru-removes-president-jose-jeri-chifagate-scandal-tied-chinese-contractor'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/18/peru-s-congress-impeaches-interim-president-jose-jeri_6750591_4.html'>Peru&#x27;s Congress impeaches interim President Jose Jeri</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/perus-congress-removes-interim-president-jose-jeri-as-he-faces-corruption-probe'>Peru&#x27;s Congress removes interim President José Jerí as he faces corruption probe</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/17/world/americas/peru-president-jose-jeri-impeachment.html'>Peru Votes to Impeach President José Jerí</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/perus-congress-debate-motion-remove-interim-president-jer-130235141'>Peru&#x27;s Congress removes interim President Jerí as he faces corruption allegations</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://time.com/7379304/peru-president-impeached-jose-jeri/'>Peru Ousts President for the Second Time in Less Than Six Months</a> - time.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/02/17/peru-s-congress-ousts-interim-president-jose-jeri'>Peru’s Congress ousts interim President José Jerí</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/peru-ousts-interim-president-over-corruption-probe/a-76013641'>Peru ousts interim president over corruption probe</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cz7gvdx457vo'>Peru&#x27;s Congress ousts president after four months in office</a> - bbc.com<